package Physics.Tests

use Libraries.Game.Layer3D
use Libraries.Interface.Item3D

/*
Tests that a box with nothing under it falls the way the physics steps say it
should. Each step first adds gravity times the step to the speed, and then
moves the box by its new speed times the step, as Bullet does. After n steps
of h seconds the box is falling at g n h, and has fallen g h h n (n + 1) / 2.

After 60 steps, 1 second, that is a speed of 9.8 and a drop of
9.8 * 1830 / 3600 = 4.98167, so a box dropped from 10 is at 5.01833. If the
steps moved the box before speeding it up, it would be at 5.18167 instead.
*/
class FreeFallTest is PhysicsWorldTest
    on create
        SetName("World: a box falls freely under gravity")
    end

    action Run
        Layer3D layer = MakeWorld()
        Item3D box = AddBox(layer, 0, 10, 0, 1, 1)

        Advance(layer, 1)

        CheckNear("falling speed after 1 second", box:GetLinearVelocity():GetY(), -9.8, 0.001)
        CheckNear("height after 1 second", box:GetY(), 5.01833, 0.001)
        CheckNear("no drift along x", box:GetX(), 0, 0.0001)
        CheckNear("no drift along z", box:GetZ(), 0, 0.0001)
        CheckNear("no turning", TurningSpeed(box), 0, 0.0001)
        CheckThat("still awake while falling", box:IsSimulated())
    end
end
